#heading(level: 1)[Complete cold DLP runtime through ecbench]
#text("Run 20261019-190253-boolean-adaptive-ecbench-cbeb18, source 9bed104b0a. Complete one-target cold DLP recovery on dedicated c7i.2xlarge; native ecbench L2 requirement, one worker,8 independent public targets per curve,5 measured rounds plus1 warmup,11 interleaved arms. Sources/specs and complete audit certificates remain adjacent/raw. Missing, failed and below-level rows are retained; a launch is not a result.")


#text("All methods within each session share the same public targets and standard polynomial subspace: dimension5 at n17 and6 at n23. These bases differ from the component experiment's Frobenius-invariant bases. The curve identities are icv1-f2m17-tm101-00378d4e and icv1-f2m23-tm5197-1f85e9e1. This two-size panel is not a scaling claim.")


#text("The pipeline solve clock includes factor-base construction, oracle prepare, relation collection, linear algebra, target descent/recovery and internal verification. Whole child process additionally includes adapter construction, report metadata, common workload construction and startup. Both clocks are recorded; the native harness's comparison gate uses the pipeline solve clock. Independent parent verification/replay, compilation and warmup are outside these clocks.")


#text("F4/F5 baseline uses the prior recursive policy with qualified GF2 kernels. Sources0acfc55b7f/71c4c99d85 use candidate matrix_runtime=quadratic-tail; corrected source9bed104b0a uses adaptive-quadratic-tail, with a different method identity. F6 names kernel_runtime=native-v1. Generalized typed roots and both Semaev table backends participate. Environment-override refusal remains intact; no admission threshold is relaxed.")


#text("Wall ratios below are B/A from ecbench's own paired bootstrap and A/A gate. Admission, completeness and outside_noise must all support a gain; partial/failed sessions do not become successful comparisons. Process medians are supplementary observed clocks, not a replacement gate.")


#text("Counted S, generic floor and matched strong rho are retained in table-n*.txt and ecbench-summary.json. Gray assignments are explicitly counted unpriced; reference native unpriced counters are retained too. Sensitivity bands at0/0.1/1 GAE per recorded operation are diagnostic and deduplicate generalized solver-count aliases. An unquantified counter stays unquantified. No ratio of lower bounds is a full-cost ranking.")


#text("Exact original-output and replay checks, query-count comparisons, source/binary hashes, failures and job resources remain in the evidence. All-L2 coverage is separate from execution/verification completeness; a fully verified session can have below-level timing rows. Low-sample clocks are descriptive; no threshold is relaxed. New matrix policies stay opt-in; no external-fastest, other-hardware or rho-beating claim is made.")


